#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:5
msgid "Making a release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:7
msgid ""
"A core developer should use the following steps to create a release ``X.Y."
"Z`` of **scikit-build** on `PyPI`_ and `Conda`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:12
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:14
msgid "All CI tests are passing on `GitHub Actions`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:16
msgid ""
"You can push to the repository and create GitHub releases. No PyPI "
"credentials are needed: publishing the GitHub release triggers a GitHub "
"Actions workflow that builds the package and uploads it to `PyPI`_ using "
"trusted publishing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:23
msgid "Documentation conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:25
msgid ""
"The commands reported below should be evaluated in the same terminal session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:27
msgid "Commands to evaluate starts with a dollar sign. For example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:29
msgid ""
"$ echo \"Hello\"\n"
"Hello"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:32
msgid ""
"means that ``echo \"Hello\"`` should be copied and evaluated in the terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:36
msgid "`PyPI`_: Step-by-step"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:38
msgid "Make sure that all CI tests are passing on `GitHub Actions`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:41
msgid "Download the latest sources (or use an existing git checkout)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:43
msgid ""
"$ cd /tmp && \\\n"
"  git clone git@github.com:scikit-build/scikit-build && \\\n"
"  cd scikit-build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:50
msgid "List all tags sorted by creation date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:52
msgid "$ git tag -l --sort creatordate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:57
msgid "Choose the next release version number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:59 ../../../make_a_release.rst:157
msgid "$ release=X.Y.Z"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:65
msgid ""
"Tags are bare :pep:`440` versions with no ``v`` prefix: ``1.0.0``, "
"``1.0.0rc1``, ``1.0.0.post1``. The version is derived from the tag by hatch-"
"vcs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:70
msgid ""
"In ``CHANGES.md`` replace ``Next Release`` section header with ``Scikit-"
"build X.Y.Z`` and commit the changes. Keep the ``START-BRIEF-CHANGELOG`` "
"marker above the newest release section so the release notes appear in the "
"PyPI readme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:75
msgid ""
"$ git add CHANGES.md && \\\n"
"  git commit -m \"Scikit-build $release\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:81
msgid "Tag the release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:83
msgid "$ git tag -a -m \"Scikit-build $release\" $release main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:88
msgid "Publish both the release tag and the main branch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:90
msgid ""
"$ git push origin $release && \\\n"
"  git push origin main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:96
msgid ""
"Make a `GitHub release <https://github.com/scikit-build/scikit-build/"
"releases/new>`_. Paste the release's section from ``CHANGES.md`` as the "
"body. The ``{pr}`` and ``{user}`` roles should be converted to simple "
"``#<number>`` and ``@<user>`` form. Be sure to use the tag you just pushed "
"as the tag version, and ``Scikit-build X.Y.Z`` should be the name. For a "
"release candidate, check the \"Set as a pre-release\" box so it does not "
"become the latest release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:105
msgid ""
"For examples of releases, see https://github.com/scikit-build/scikit-build/"
"releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:107
msgid ""
"Publishing the release triggers the ``CD`` GitHub Actions workflow, which "
"builds the SDist and wheel and uploads them to `PyPI`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:111
msgid ""
"Add a ``Next Release`` section back in ``CHANGES.md``, commit and push local "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:113
msgid ""
"$ git add CHANGES.md && \\\n"
"  git commit -m \"CHANGES.md: Add \\\"Next Release\\\" section [ci skip]\" "
"&& \\\n"
"  git push origin main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:121
msgid ""
"Add an entry to the ``Announcements`` category of the `scikit-build "
"discussions board`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:125
msgid ""
"For examples of announcements, see https://github.com/orgs/scikit-build/"
"discussions/categories/announcements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:136
msgid "`Conda`_: Step-by-step"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:140
msgid "Publishing on conda requires the corresponding GitHub release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:142
msgid ""
"After a GitHub release is created in the `scikit-build <https://github.com/"
"scikit-build/scikit-build>`_ project and after the conda-forge `Autoticking "
"Bot <https://justcalamari.github.io/jekyll/update/2018/06/11/introduction."
"html>`_ creates a pull request on the `scikit-build-feedstock`_ , follow "
"these steps to finalize the conda package release:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:147
msgid "Review the pull-request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:149
msgid "Merge pull-request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:152
msgid ""
"In case the bot failed (e.g because of GH rate limitation) and in order to "
"explicitly release a new version on conda-forge, follow the steps below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:155
msgid ""
"Choose the next release version number (that matches with the PyPI version "
"last published)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:161
msgid "Fork scikit-build-feedstock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:163
msgid ""
"First step is to fork `scikit-build-feedstock`_ repository. This is the "
"recommended `best practice <https://conda-forge.org/docs/maintainer/"
"updating_pkgs.html>`_  by conda."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:167
msgid "Clone forked feedstock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:169
msgid "Fill the YOURGITHUBUSER part."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:171
msgid ""
"$ YOURGITHUBUSER=user\n"
"$ cd /tmp && git clone https://github.com/$YOURGITHUBUSER/scikit-build-"
"feedstock.git"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:177
msgid "Download corresponding source for the release version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:179
msgid ""
"$ cd /tmp && \\\n"
"  wget https://github.com/scikit-build/scikit-build/archive/$release.tar.gz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:185
msgid "Create a new branch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:187
msgid ""
"$ cd scikit-build-feedstock && \\\n"
"  git checkout -b $release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:193
msgid "Modify ``meta.yaml``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:195
msgid ""
"Update the `version string <https://github.com/conda-forge/scikit-build-"
"feedstock/blob/main/recipe/meta.yaml#L2>`_ and `sha256 <https://github.com/"
"conda-forge/scikit-build-feedstock/blob/main/recipe/meta.yaml#L3>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:198
msgid ""
"We have to modify the sha and the version string in the ``meta.yaml`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:200
msgid "For linux flavors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:202
msgid ""
"$ sed -i \"1s/.*/{% set version = \\\"$release\\\" %}/\" recipe/meta.yaml && "
"\\\n"
"  sha=$(openssl sha256 /tmp/$release.tar.gz | awk '{print $2}') && \\\n"
"  sed -i \"2s/.*/{% set sha256 = \\\"$sha\\\" %}/\" recipe/meta.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:208
msgid "For macOS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:210
msgid ""
"$ sed -i -- \"1s/.*/{% set version = \\\"$release\\\" %}/\" recipe/meta.yaml "
"&& \\\n"
"  sha=$(openssl sha256 /tmp/$release.tar.gz | awk '{print $2}') && \\\n"
"  sed -i -- \"2s/.*/{% set sha256 = \\\"$sha\\\" %}/\" recipe/meta.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:216
msgid "Commit local changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:218
msgid ""
"$ git add recipe/meta.yaml && \\\n"
"    git commit -m \"scikit-build v$release version\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:224
msgid "Push the changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:226
msgid "$ git push origin $release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:230
msgid "Create a Pull Request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../make_a_release.rst:232
msgid ""
"Create a pull request against the `main repository <https://github.com/conda-"
"forge/scikit-build-feedstock/pulls>`_. If the tests are passed a new release "
"will be published on Anaconda cloud."
msgstr ""
